 "drivingQuestion": "How can the baraita include the mules when the mishna excludes them?",
 "outcome": "resolved",
 "outcomeNote": "baraita retained by limiting it to fastened mules",
 "continuesQuestionOf": null,
 "segments": [
  {
   "id": "bava_batra.77b.6",
   "daf": "77b",
   "sentenceId": 5,
   "he": "גְּמָ׳ תָּנֵי רַב תַּחְלִיפָא בַּר מַעְרְבָא קַמֵּיהּ דְּרַבִּי אֲבָהוּ: מָכַר אֶת הַקָּרוֹן – מָכַר אֶת הַפְּרָדוֹת. וְהָא אֲנַן ״לֹא מָכַר״ תְּנַן! אֲמַר לֵיהּ: אִיסְמְיַיהּ? אֲמַר לֵיהּ: לָא, תִּיתַּרְגֵּם מַתְנִיתָיךְ בַּאֲדוּקִין בּוֹ.",
   "en": "«GEMARA:» «Rav Taḥlifa, from the West,» i.e., Eretz Yisrael, «taught» a baraita «before Rabbi Abbahu.» If one «sold a wagon, he has sold the mules» together with it. Rabbi Abbahu asked: «But didn’t we learn» in the mishna that «he has not sold» the mules? Rav Taḥlifa «said to him:» Should «I erase» this baraita, as it is incorrect? Rabbi Abbahu «said to him: No,» do not erase it; you should «explain» that «your baraita» is referring to a case «where» the mules «are fastened to» the wagon. In that situation, one who purchases the wagon receives the mules as well."
  }
 ],
